    <hr>

    <main>

        <section id="english">

            <h2>
                Technical Explanation — English
            </h2>

            <p>
                AI development tools can improve productivity, but many
                of them are not completely free.
            </p>

            <p>
                Some services may offer:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    A free trial
                </li>

                <li>
                    A limited free plan
                </li>

                <li>
                    A small number of monthly requests
                </li>

                <li>
                    Access to fewer AI models
                </li>

                <li>
                    Reduced speed or fewer features
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                These free options may be useful for learning,
                experimenting, or testing a tool.
            </p>

            <p>
                However, regular professional use may require a paid
                subscription.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Why AI Tools Cost Money
            </h2>

            <p>
                AI systems require powerful computer infrastructure.
            </p>

            <p>
                When a developer sends a prompt, the service may need to:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    Receive the request.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Process the prompt.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Read project context.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Run an AI model.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Generate a response.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Send the result back to the user.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <p>
                This process uses servers, electricity, networking,
                storage, security systems, and technical support.
            </p>

            <p>
                Therefore, service providers often charge users when
                usage becomes frequent or advanced.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Free Plans and Paid Plans
            </h2>

            <table border="1">

                <thead>

                    <tr>
                        <th>Plan Type</th>
                        <th>Possible Benefits</th>
                        <th>Possible Limitations</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            Free plan
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Useful for testing and basic learning
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Limited prompts, features, speed, or models
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            Paid plan
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Higher limits, more features, and more
                            reliable access
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Monthly or yearly cost
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            Team plan
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Shared administration, controls, and team
                            features
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Higher cost and account-management needs
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

            <p>
                The exact plans may differ between providers.
            </p>

            <p>
                Students should always read the current pricing,
                limitations, and cancellation rules before subscribing.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Budgeting for AI Tools
            </h2>

            <p>
                Developers should treat AI subscriptions like other
                professional tools.
            </p>

            <p>
                Before paying, ask:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Do I use this tool regularly?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Does it save meaningful time?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Does it improve my work quality?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Can one tool replace another subscription?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Is the monthly cost affordable?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Can I cancel easily?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Does the plan include the features I need?
                </li>
            </ul>

            <article>

                <h3>
                    EGA Budget Principle
                </h3>

                <p>
                    Do not pay for an AI tool only because it is popular.
                    Pay when it gives clear value to your learning or
                    development work.
                </p>

            </article>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                AI Results Are Not Always Identical
            </h2>

            <p>
                AI tools may produce different answers even when two
                users enter similar prompts.
            </p>

            <p>
                Results may change because of:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Different wording in the prompt
                </li>

                <li>
                    Different project files
                </li>

                <li>
                    Different account settings
                </li>

                <li>
                    Different AI models
                </li>

                <li>
                    Changes made by the service provider
                </li>

                <li>
                    Different conversation history
                </li>

                <li>
                    Different software versions
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Therefore, students should not expect every generated
                answer to match a course demonstration exactly.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                AI Models Change Over Time
            </h2>

            <p>
                AI providers regularly update their systems.
            </p>

            <p>
                A newer model may:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Understand instructions better
                </li>

                <li>
                    Generate different code
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use a different writing style
                </li>

                <li>
                    Support longer project context
                </li>

                <li>
                    Include new features
                </li>

                <li>
                    Remove or rename older features
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                The interface of GitHub Copilot, Cursor, ChatGPT, or
                another AI service may also change after a lesson is
                created.
            </p>

            <p>
                Students should focus on the method and principles,
                rather than memorizing one exact screen or response.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Focus on the Workflow, Not the Exact Output
            </h2>

            <p>
                The main purpose of an AI-development lesson is to teach
                a repeatable workflow.
            </p>

            <p>
                A useful workflow is:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    Understand the development task.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Choose the correct AI tool.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Write a clear prompt.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Add useful context.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Review the generated result.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Test the code.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Correct errors.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Save the verified solution.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <p>
                Even when the AI produces a different response, the same
                review and testing process still applies.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Example: Different Results from Similar Prompts
            </h2>

            <p>
                Consider these two prompts:
            </p>

            <blockquote>
                Create an HTML registration form.
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote>
                Create a beginner-friendly HTML student-registration
                form with name, email, phone, course selection, labels,
                required fields, and a submit button.
            </blockquote>

            <p>
                The second prompt contains more detail.
            </p>

            <p>
                It is likely to produce a more specific result because
                the AI has clearer requirements.
            </p>

            <p>
                This shows that prompt quality can affect output quality.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Never Depend on One Generated Result
            </h2>

            <p>
                A developer should not assume that the first AI response
                is the final answer.
            </p>

            <p>
                A better approach is to:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Read the response carefully
                </li>

                <li>
                    Ask follow-up questions
                </li>

                <li>
                    Request corrections
                </li>

                <li>
                    Compare possible solutions
                </li>

                <li>
                    Test the code
                </li>

                <li>
                    Keep a working backup
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                AI assistance is an interactive process, not a guarantee
                of perfect output.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Safe Subscription Practices
            </h2>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Confirm the official provider before paying.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Read whether the price is monthly or yearly.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Check whether taxes are added.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Understand automatic renewal.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Save payment receipts.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use a strong password.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Enable two-factor authentication when available.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Cancel unused subscriptions.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Never share an account password with students.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="html-learning">

            <h2>
                HTML Learning in This Lesson
            </h2>

            <p>
                This lesson uses HTML to teach both AI concepts and
                webpage structure.
            </p>

            <p>
                Important HTML features in this lesson include:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    The <strong>&lt;meta&gt;</strong> element
                </li>

                <li>
                    The <strong>name</strong> attribute
                </li>

                <li>
                    The <strong>content</strong> attribute
                </li>

                <li>
                    The <strong>&lt;article&gt;</strong> element
                </li>

                <li>
                    The <strong>&lt;blockquote&gt;</strong> element
                </li>

                <li>
                    Table elements
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                The Meta Description Element
            </h2>

            <p>
                A meta description provides a short description of a
                webpage.
            </p>

            <h3>
                HTML Code
            </h3>

            <pre><code>&lt;meta
    name="description"
    content="A lesson about AI tool costs and changing results."
&gt;</code></pre>

            <p>
                The <strong>&lt;meta&gt;</strong> element is placed
                inside the <strong>&lt;head&gt;</strong>.
            </p>

            <p>
                It does not use a closing tag.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>name="description"</strong> identifies the
                    type of metadata.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>content</strong> contains the webpage
                    description.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                The meta description does not normally appear inside the
                visible webpage body.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                The Head and Body Difference
            </h2>

            <p>
                The <strong>&lt;head&gt;</strong> contains information
                about the webpage.
            </p>

            <p>
                The <strong>&lt;body&gt;</strong> contains content that
                users see in the browser.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;head&gt;

    &lt;title&gt;
        Lesson 4
    &lt;/title&gt;

    &lt;meta
        name="description"
        content="Lesson description"
    &gt;

&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;

    &lt;h1&gt;
        Visible Lesson Title
    &lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>

            <h3>
                Browser Output
            </h3>

            <p>
                The title may appear in the browser tab.
            </p>

            <p>
                The heading appears inside the visible webpage.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                The Table Element Reminder
            </h2>

            <p>
                The plan comparison uses a table.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;table border="1"&gt;

    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;th&gt;Plan&lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;th&gt;Limit&lt;/th&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;

    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;Free&lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td&gt;Limited usage&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre>

            <h3>
                Browser Output
            </h3>

            <table border="1">

                <tr>
                    <th>Plan</th>
                    <th>Limit</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Free</td>
                    <td>Limited usage</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Image Path Reminder
            </h2>

            <p>
                The EGA logo uses:
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;img
    src="images/ega-logo.png"
    alt="Elmi Guray Academy logo"
    width="180"
&gt;</code></pre>

            <p>
                The image works because
                <strong>ega-logo.png</strong>
                is stored inside the
                <strong>images</strong> folder.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Important Rules
            </h2>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Free access may have usage limits.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Regular professional use may require payment.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Check current pricing before subscribing.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not pay for tools you do not use.
                </li>

                <li>
                    AI results may differ between users.
                </li>

                <li>
                    AI models and interfaces may change.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Focus on the workflow, not one exact response.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Review and test all generated code.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Save receipts and monitor recurring subscriptions.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Never share passwords or payment details.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Common Beginner Mistakes
            </h2>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Assuming every AI tool is permanently free
                </li>

                <li>
                    Forgetting about automatic renewal
                </li>

                <li>
                    Paying before testing the free plan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Expecting exactly the same AI answer as another user
                </li>

                <li>
                    Copying an AI response without testing it
                </li>

                <li>
                    Believing an old course interface will never change
                </li>

                <li>
                    Paying for several overlapping tools
                </li>

                <li>
                    Ignoring monthly subscription costs
                </li>

                <li>
                    Using the wrong image path in HTML
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="somali">

            <h2>
                Farsamo — Somali
            </h2>

            <p>
                AI tools badan oo developers isticmaalaan si buuxda
                bilaash uma aha.
            </p>

            <p>
                Qaar waxay leeyihiin:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Free trial
                </li>

                <li>
                    Free plan xaddidan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Tiro prompts ah oo kooban
                </li>

                <li>
                    Features yar
                </li>

                <li>
                    Speed ama model xaddidan
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Free plan-ku wuxuu ku fiican yahay barashada iyo
                tijaabinta.
            </p>

            <p>
                Laakiin marka tool-ka si joogto ah loo isticmaalo,
                paid plan ayaa loo baahan karaa.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Sababta AI Tools-ku Lacag u Yihiin
            </h2>

            <p>
                AI systems-ku waxay isticmaalaan computers awood badan,
                servers, internet, storage, electricity, iyo security.
            </p>

            <p>
                Markaad prompt dirto, system-ku waa inuu codsiga
                farsameeyaa oo jawaab kuu soo saaraa.
            </p>

            <p>
                Taasi waxay provider-ka ku leedahay kharash.
            </p>

            <p>
                Sidaas darteed usage badan badanaa lacag ayuu u baahan
                yahay.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Free Plan iyo Paid Plan
            </h2>

            <p>
                Free plan-ku wuxuu kuu oggolaan karaa inaad tool-ka
                tijaabiso.
            </p>

            <p>
                Laakiin waxaa jiri kara xaddidaad sida:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Prompts yar
                </li>

                <li>
                    Models kooban
                </li>

                <li>
                    Features xaddidan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Speed gaabis ah
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Paid plan-ku wuxuu bixin karaa usage badan iyo features
                dheeraad ah.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Natiijooyinka AI Isku Mid Ma Aha
            </h2>

            <p>
                Laba qof oo isticmaalaya prompt isku dhow waxay heli
                karaan jawaabo kala duwan.
            </p>

            <p>
                Sababaha waxaa ka mid noqon kara:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Prompt wording kala duwan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Project context kala duwan
                </li>

                <li>
                    AI model kala duwan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Software version kala duwan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Conversation history kala duwan
                </li>

                <li>
                    Provider update cusub
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Sidaas darteed ardaygu waa inuusan filan in jawaabtiisu
                si buuxda ula mid noqoto tusaalaha macallinka.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Diiradda Saar Habka Shaqada
            </h2>

            <p>
                Waxa ugu muhiimsan ma aha hal jawaab oo AI soo saaro.
            </p>

            <p>
                Waxa muhiimka ahi waa inaad barato habka:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    Faham task-ga.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Dooro tool-ka saxda ah.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Qor prompt cad.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Sii context ku filan.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Akhri jawaabta.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Tijaabi code-ka.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Sax khaladaadka.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Keydi version-ka la xaqiijiyey.
                </li>
            </ol>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Xeerka Lacag-bixinta
            </h2>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Hubi provider-ka rasmiga ah.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Akhri qiimaha monthly ama yearly.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Hubi automatic renewal.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Keydi receipt-ka.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Jooji subscription-ka aadan isticmaalin.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Ha wadaagin password-ka.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Ha bixin lacag ilaa aad fahanto plan-ka.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="gal">

            <h2>
                GAL — General Analogy Learning — English
            </h2>

            <p>
                Imagine using mobile internet.
            </p>

            <p>
                A network provider may give you a small free amount of
                data to begin.
            </p>

            <p>
                That may be enough to test messaging or browse a few
                pages.
            </p>

            <p>
                But if you watch videos, download files, and use the
                internet every day, you need a larger paid data plan.
            </p>

            <p>
                AI tools work in a similar way.
            </p>

            <p>
                Limited free access may be enough for testing, but
                frequent professional use may require payment.
            </p>

            <p>
                Also, internet speed and results can change depending on
                the network, device, and location.
            </p>

            <p>
                AI answers can also change depending on the model,
                prompt, context, and software version.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                GAL — Somali
            </h2>

            <p>
                Ka fikir mobile internet.
            </p>

            <p>
                Shirkadda network-ku waxay ku siin kartaa data yar oo
                bilaash ah si aad u tijaabiso.
            </p>

            <p>
                Data-gaas wuxuu ku filnaan karaa fariimo ama bogag yar.
            </p>

            <p>
                Laakiin haddii aad maalin kasta daawato videos oo aad
                files soo dejiso, waxaad u baahan tahay package lacag
                leh.
            </p>

            <p>
                AI tools-kuna sidaas oo kale ayay u shaqeeyaan.
            </p>

            <p>
                Free plan yar wuxuu ku filnaan karaa tijaabo, laakiin
                usage joogto ah wuxuu u baahan karaa paid plan.
            </p>

            <p>
                Sida internet-ku u kala duwanaan karo, jawaabaha AI-na
                way kala duwanaan karaan iyadoo ku xiran model-ka,
                prompt-ka, context-ka, iyo version-ka.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="activity">

            <h2>
                Multiple-Choice Practice Activity
            </h2>

            <form>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        1. Why may AI tools require payment?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question1"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        AI systems use expensive computer infrastructure
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question1"
                            value="b"
                        >
                        AI tools do not use any computers
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question1"
                            value="c"
                        >
                        Payment is required only to change screen color
                    </label>

                </fieldset>

                <br>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        2. What is a possible limitation of a free plan?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question2"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        Limited prompts or features
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question2"
                            value="b"
                        >
                        Unlimited use forever
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question2"
                            value="c"
                        >
                        It repairs the computer physically
                    </label>

                </fieldset>

                <br>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        3. Why may AI results differ?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question3"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        Prompts, models, context, and versions may differ
